# A top-level `fn` is bound once (field build §1.59): a second definition of the same name
# is refused before anything runs, naming the first — as `x = 1` then `x = 2` is refused.
# The first used to win in silence: a test asserted against a function three lines above
# the one it defined, and nothing said so.
fn tag(n) = "X-{n}"
# a comment between them, as in the file that found it
fn tag(v) = "X-Tag"
print(tag(1))
